# Important Definitions

### OSI Model

A 7-layer model explaining network communication.

---

### TCP/IP Model

The real-world networking model used on the Internet.

---

### TCP

Reliable protocol that guarantees packet delivery.

---

### UDP

Fast protocol without delivery guarantees.

---

### Port

A logical communication endpoint used by applications and services.

Example:

```
80 → HTTP

443 → HTTPS
```

---

### Router

A Layer 3 device that forwards packets using **IP Addresses**.

---

### Switch

A Layer 2 device that forwards frames using **MAC Addresses**.

---

### Hub

A Layer 1 device that broadcasts incoming data to all connected devices.

